task: depth-is-policy-not-rescue
agent: opus-depth
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/depth-is-policy-not-rescue
worktree: ../okay-wt-policy-spec
spec: specs/iterative-recursive-decode.md (extended, not rewritten)

why: the operator asked "why do we still need Codecs.maxDepth — can
  we remove it?" The honest answer, checked in code before answering:
  no, not yet. Four native-recursion sites are STILL protected only by
  the hard Codecs.maxDepth refusal, never given the threshold+trampoline
  treatment either root got: JsonValue's fast parser (array/object
  literal nesting), Json.lossless's projection (`into`/`pairs`),
  JsonStrict.Reader.get (product/array/sum descent), and Cbor.In.skipItem
  (skipping an undeclared field). Any one of them would still overflow
  on the ORIGINAL input-depth-both-wires shape if Codecs.maxDepth were
  raised or removed.

what: extend specs/iterative-recursive-decode.md with these four as
  named targets, reusing the proven design (native to a small
  threshold, Cont.defer past it) where the recursion combines
  differently-typed values (JsonStrict.Reader.get, matching root
  1/2's shape exactly), and noting where a SIMPLER fix applies because
  the recursion is already uniformly typed (JsonValue's parser always
  returns Json, Cbor.In.skipItem always returns Either[String,Unit] —
  no cross-type R-threading complexity, Cont.defer still the
  mechanism but the code is more direct) or side-effects into a
  Builder rather than combining values (Json.lossless's `into`, the
  one case that may want a genuinely different shape — decided in
  that lane, not assumed here).

  Four follow-up implementation lanes, one per target, each with its
  own claim/tests/JMH gate (3 forks from the start) exactly as
  cbor-decode-threshold-trampoline and json-decode-threshold-
  -trampoline did. This claim covers ONLY the spec extension.

predict: once all four land, Codecs.maxDepth becomes a pure wire-
  -contract policy number with no stack-safety motivation left, and
  removing it (or setting it very high) becomes a deliberate,
  low-risk choice rather than reopening input-depth-both-wires.
